This paper sits between KUNDO/PDEDER (3.25–5.25) in quality. It has a better problem framing and cleaner pipeline than KUNDO, and stronger PDE results than PDEDER, but shares the same class of weaknesses: critical ablation gap for the core technical contribution (ESRL), overclaimed zero-shot generalization without demonstration, and weak baselines for one experimental setting. The SALEM module results provide genuine evidence of improvement. Overall, the paper is below the acceptance threshold due to the unsupported ESRL contribution and unverified zero-shot claim, but not as weak as the truly poor papers in the <3 range.

