Hi-IR is clearly better than MetaFormer (2.5) and DyNet (4.0) due to comprehensive empirical validation across 7 tasks with competitive results. It is comparable to Key-Graph (5.75) in terms of architectural contribution and SOTA consistency, but Hi-IR has broader task coverage and a more systematic scaling analysis. It falls below RGT (7.5) because RGT had cleaner claims matched to evidence and stronger novelty within its scope. The major weakness is the overclaimed generalizability (the third contribution in the introduction is not actually validated) and the overstated SOTA claim. These are significant but don't invalidate the core architectural contribution.

