| DetEmbedMetrics | OdoS6cH8MP.md | 2.0 | Weak benchmark with synthetic-only evaluation. MentalChat16K is significantly better than this. |

MentalChat16K falls between medium and low anchors. It has a real contribution (the dataset, the evaluation bias finding) but significant methodological concerns (LLM-processed "real" data, GPT-4 evaluation bias, no clinical validation). It is notably stronger than the rejected mental-health LLM papers (MentalArena at 4.0, pSAE-chiatry at 2.5) because it includes real data, multiple evaluation modalities, and honest reporting of negative findings. It is notably weaker than accepted benchmark papers (WildBench at 7.33, CENTaUR at 8.0) because of the evaluation methodology gaps and the overclaimed "real" data framing.

